{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetMZtVfrkR96gLMsLv7m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me summarize my analysis findings:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order.kt:11-16 — Order is a simple data class without status field\n- OrderController.kt:17-46 — OrderController handles create, getById, list\n- OrderRepository.kt:11-27 — InMemoryOrderRepository with save, existsById, findById, findAll, clear\n- Shipment.kt:9-14 — Shipment already has status field (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentController.kt:22-56 — ShipmentController handles create, getById, list\n- ShipmentRepository.kt:11-27 — InMemoryShipmentRepository lacks findByOrderId method\n- ApiExceptions.kt:18-30 — Two exception classes: ResourceNotFoundException (404), ConflictException (409)\n- ApiError.kt:31-37 — ErrorCode enum currently has ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED\n- GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:14-28 — Central handler that wraps all ApiExceptions into ApiError envelope\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n- No separate service layer; logic lives in controllers\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses; GlobalExceptionHandler catches them\n- Tests use MockMvc and assert on response **bodies**, not just status codes\n- Tests verify error envelope structure (error.code, error.message)\n- Both Order and Shipment repositories follow identical patterns: save, existsById, findById, findAll, clear\n- In-memory repositories use ConcurrentHashMap\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. Order.kt — must add status field and OrderStatus enum\n2. OrderController.kt — must add POST cancel endpoint and check shipment states\n3. ShipmentRepository.kt — must add findByOrderId method to query shipments for an order\n4. ApiError.kt — must add error codes for new cancellation failures (ORDER_CANCELLED, SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED_BLOCKS_CANCEL)\n5. OrderControllerTest.kt — must add tests for all five cancellation scenarios\n\n**Risks:**\n- Serializing Order with a new status field may break tests that don't explicitly check for it\n- Shipment confirmation logic (BE-003) may already exist and interact with order cancellation\n- Concurrent modifications to order and shipments in same transaction could lose updates in-memory\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone; the requirement defines all five cases (successful cancel, repeated cancel, confirmed-shipment conflict, not-found, shipment-create-on-cancelled-order).\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add `status: OrderStatus` field to Order data class. Add `OrderStatus` enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED. Update CreateOrderRequest to omit status (always ACTIVE on creation).\n\n2. **OrderController.kt**: Add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` method that:\n   - Gets the order, throws 404 if not found\n   - If already CANCELLED, return 200 with unchanged order\n   - Check all shipments for this order; if any is CONFIRMED, throw 409 (ConflictException) with no changes made\n   - Change order status to CANCELLED, change all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED, save both\n   - Return 200 with updated order\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method that filters store by orderId.\n\n4. **ApiError.kt**: Add two error codes:\n   - `ORDER_CANCELLED` — trying to cancel an order that is already CANCELLED (actually succeeds, so not needed for error)\n   - `SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED` — a shipment for this order is CONFIRMED, blocking the cancel\n\n5. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add four new test methods:\n   - `cancels an active order and updates its status` — creates order, cancels it, verifies status changed to CANCELLED, verifies with GET that it persisted\n   - `cancels all CREATED shipments of a cancelled order` — creates order, creates CREATED shipment, cancels order, verifies shipment is now CANCELLED\n   - `repeated cancel succeeds` — cancels order, cancels again, verifies success and no change\n   - `cancel blocked by CONFIRMED shipment` — creates order, creates shipment, manually confirms it, cancels order, expects 409, verifies order and shipment unchanged with GET\n   - `cancel unknown order returns 404` — cancels non-existent order, verifies 404 with error code\n   - (Bonus) Test that creating a shipment for CANCELLED order fails with 409 — this test goes in ShipmentControllerTest.kt\n\n**Alternative approaches rejected:**\n\n1. **Service layer approach** — Could add OrderCancellationService, but this would be inconsistent with existing codebase which has no service layer. Rejected to maintain convention.\n\n2. **Soft delete on Order** — Could just set a flag instead of adding OrderStatus enum, but using an explicit enum is more type-safe and matches Shipment's pattern.\n\n3. **Immediate shipment cancellation in database transaction** — Would require a transaction manager, but the baseline uses in-memory concurrent maps. Keeping it simple by updating both in controller.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Successful cancel of ACTIVE order:*\n- POST /orders/O-1/cancel\n- Read order from repository, status is ACTIVE\n- Query all shipments with orderId=O-1\n- None have CONFIRMED status\n- Update order.status = CANCELLED\n- Update all shipments with status CREATED → CANCELLED\n- Save both order and shipments\n- Return 200 with updated order\n\n*Repeat cancel (already CANCELLED):*\n- POST /orders/O-1/cancel (second time)\n- Read order from repository, status is CANCELLED\n- Query all shipments with orderId=O-1\n- Return 200 with unchanged order (no-op)\n\n*Cancel blocked by CONFIRMED shipment:*\n- POST /orders/O-1/cancel\n- Read order from repository, status is ACTIVE\n- Query all shipments with orderId=O-1\n- One has status CONFIRMED\n- Throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED code\n- Transaction rolls back; order and all shipments unchanged\n- Return 409 with error envelope\n\n*Cancel non-existent order:*\n- POST /orders/O-999/cancel\n- Read order from repository, returns null\n- Throw ResourceNotFoundException with ORDER_NOT_FOUND code\n- Return 404 with error envelope\n\n*Create shipment on CANCELLED order:*\n- POST /shipments with orderId=O-1 (which is CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentController.create() must check order status\n- Order repository.findById(orderId) returns order with status CANCELLED\n- Throw ConflictException with ORDER_CANCELLED code\n- Return 409 with error envelope\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **`cancels_active_order_and_persists_status`** — Create order O-1, cancel it, assert response body has status CANCELLED, GET /orders/O-1, assert persisted status is CANCELLED\n2. **`cancel_cancels_created_shipments`** — Create order O-1, create shipment S-1 (status CREATED), cancel order, GET /shipments/S-1, assert status is CANCELLED\n3. **`repeated_cancel_succeeds`** — Cancel O-1, cancel O-1 again, assert second response status 200 and body unchanged\n4. **`cancel_blocked_by_confirmed_shipment`** — Create O-1, create S-1, manually set S-1 to CONFIRMED (via repository in test setup), cancel O-1, expect 409 with SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED code, GET /orders/O-1 and GET /shipments/S-1, assert both unchanged\n5. **`cancel_unknown_order_returns_404`** — Cancel O-999, expect 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND code\n6. **`shipment_create_on_cancelled_order_fails`** — (in ShipmentControllerTest) Create O-1, cancel O-1, POST shipment for O-1, expect 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":241,"cache_read_input_tokens":24586,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":241},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id"