ry per requirement.\n- **ApiError.kt** — Added SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED and ORDER_CANCELLED error codes. Necessary for API contract.\n- **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Added 6 comprehensive tests covering all cancel scenarios, following the testing-and-verification skill pattern (response body assertions, second GET requests to verify state).\n- **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added 1 test covering shipment creation rejection for cancelled orders, with second request to verify no shipment was created.\n\n**Unresolved findings:**\n\nNone. All acceptance criteria are met.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement: Implement `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that allows customers to cancel orders before any shipment is confirmed, with proper status tracking and all-or-nothing semantics.\n\nChanged:\n- **Order.kt** — Added `status: OrderStatus` field with ACTIVE/CANCELLED enum values\n- **OrderController.kt** — Added cancel endpoint with state validation and shipment cascade logic\n- **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Added findByOrderId query method to support cancel logic\n- **ShipmentController.kt** — Added order status check to prevent shipment creation on cancelled orders\n- **ApiError.kt** — Added SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED and ORDER_CANCELLED error codes\n- **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Added 6 tests: cancel active order, cascade cancel shipments, repeated cancel, blocked by confirmed shipment, unknown order, with response body and second GET assertions\n- **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added 1 test: reject shipment creation for cancelled order with second GET verification\n\nTests:\n- `cancels_active_order_and_persists_status` — POST /orders/O-1/cancel succeeds, response shows CANCELLED, GET /orders/O-1 persists it\n- `cancel_cancels_all_created_shipments_of_the_order` — Shipments with status CREATED are transitioned to CANCELLED when order is cancelled\n- `repeated_cancel_succeeds_and_changes_nothing` — Calling cancel twice on already-cancelled order succeeds both times